Author: Daniel Romero-Mujalli [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Daniel Romero-Mujalli <daniel.romero@supsi.ch>
Description: the package provides methods for performing start-to-finish conservation planning on freshwater systems. This includes, methods for: obtaining a Digital Elevation Model (DEM) for the extent of interest, extraction of the associated river network, delineation of the sub-basin polygons with connectivity attributes, delineation of the modelling region, training, assessment and projection of species distribution models, conservation planning. The package can execute conservation planning exercises using the software marxan from the R environment. It also provides methods to prepare marxan input data, calibrate the BLM input parameter, and get the best marxan solution.
